+## 5. Model judgements that are not in the pure predicate
+
+Listed so nothing is lost; none of them writes text that becomes a claim any more.
+
+| judgement | today | under select_by_id |
+|---|---|---|
+| the same current development across channels | adjudicate (CURRENT_EVENT + verbatim quote + chunk id) + verify_support (SUPPORTS) per video against the model-written event | the story call's choice of ids; members are verbatim by construction. An independent check MAY still run on the claim sentence (verify_support with the claim as the event: its `presented_as` = current is the useful half) |
+| currentness | transcript_currentness over adjudicated verdicts | the story call is asked for a CURRENT development; source age is deterministic (S5) |
+| Bitcoin relevance / importance | derive_story_query ratings (BTC_RELEVANCE_MIN 3) | the claim must name Bitcoin (G5); importance may still rank candidates as a label (no text from it becomes a claim) |
+| clip quality floors | rate_passages: hook >= 4.0, clip >= 3.5 | the line-up call's choice; the integrator may keep rate_passages on the chosen verbatim ranges as an independent floor (DEC-13 kept hook >= 4.0 unchanged) |
+| D4 (c) reaction / consequence | verify_reaction per added sentence | the line-up call's range choice; the integrator may keep verify_reaction on each non-statement sentence of a range |
+| editorial review / gate, stand-alone at validate | editorial_review + editorial_gate; stand_alone.check_edl | unchanged (downstream of the EDL) |
